	"department": "ENGL",
	"description": [
		"Set in Otepoti/Dunedin - where coastlines, hills, and histories converge - this course introduces creative writing as a practice of attention and connection. Through poetry, fiction, and nonfiction, students explore language, place, and identity while engaging with Aotearoa New Zealand's voices. Workshops, readings, and field visits to sites such as the Otago Peninsula and Botanic Gardens support students in developing their creative voices within a collaborative community of writers. Offered alternate years during January term."
	],
